#
# A board that has Bluetooth and no Wi-Fi: the nRF5340 DK. Its board type and flash layout are in
# Kconfig, next to the nRF7002 DK's. See "The nRF5340 DK (Bluetooth only)" in firmware/README.md.
#

config APP_BT_ONLY
	bool "Bluetooth only: no Wi-Fi, no AWS IoT"
	depends on APP_BT_OTA
	help
	  For a board with no Wi-Fi chip. prj_bt_only.conf turns it on for the nRF5340 DK. The main loop
	  is src/bt_only/bt_only_main.c in place of main.c, and the update manager src/bt_only/bt_only_ota.c in place of
	  ota.c: no network stack, no connection to AWS IoT, no jobs, no device shadow, no heartbeat, no
	  events and no location. The board updates over Bluetooth from a phone, or over USB, and an image
	  on trial is kept only by a person, as "proof: person" in firmware/README.md says.

if APP_BT_ONLY

config APP_BT_STATIC_PASSKEY
	bool "A passkey of its own for pairing, stored at provisioning"
	default y
	select BT_APP_PASSKEY
	help
	  The phone has no device shadow to get a fresh passkey from, so the board keeps one 6-digit
	  passkey in TF-M's protected storage, which tools/provision_device.py --board nrf5340dk draws at
	  random and registers with the console. It is never shown on the console. Without one, or once it
	  is locked, the Bluetooth host draws a new passkey for each attempt and the console shows it, as
	  on an offline nRF7002 DK. src/bt/bt_passkey.h says what this costs.

config APP_BT_PASSKEY_FAILURE_BUDGET
	int "Failed pairings that the stored passkey survives"
	depends on APP_BT_STATIC_PASSKEY
	default 3
	range 1 20
	help
	  A guess at a passkey that does not change, which fails, gives away the bit it failed on and
	  every bit it got right before that: two on average. After this many failures with it, counted
	  from when it was stored and across windows and restarts, the board stops using it until a new
	  one is stored. An attacker who guesses from the start pairs before that with a chance of 0.02%
	  at 3, 0.13% at 4 and 2% at 6, against 0.0003% for three tries at a new passkey each time. Three
	  failures in one window close the window, whatever this is.

endif # APP_BT_ONLY
